          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.09,
            0.765,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.7 Further Applications of the Baudhāyana-Pythagoras Theorem"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.149,
            0.846,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Baudhāyana-Pythagoras theorem is one of the fundamental theorems of geometry. Let us see some of its applications."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.202,
            0.668,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Problem from Bhāskarāchārya’s Līlāvatī"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.233,
            0.846,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The following is a translation of a problem from Bhāskarāchārya’s (Bhāskara II) Līlāvatī. Try to visualise what you read."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.282,
            0.506,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ “In a lake surrounded by chakra and krauñcha birds, there is a lotus flower peeping out of the water, with the tip of its stem 1 unit above the water. On being swayed by a gentle breeze, the tip touches the water 3 units away from its original position. Quickly tell the depth of the lake.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.453,
            0.508,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "At first glance, it seems like there is insufficient data to find the solution. But the solution exists!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.52,
            0.287,
            0.902,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.52,
                0.287,
                0.902,
                0.477
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.508,
            0.846,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let x be the length of the stem inside the water. This is the required depth of the lake. Since the stem of the lotus is sticking 1 unit above the water, the total length of the stem is x + 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.563,
            0.847,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can make a (very reasonable) assumption that the lotus stem is perpendicular to the surface of the water in the first position. With this assumption, we get a right triangle of sides 3, x and x + 1. As this satisfies the Baudhāyana-Pythagoras theorem, we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.64,
            0.575,
            0.661
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "3^{2}+x^{2}=(x+1)^{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.67,
            0.587,
            0.69
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "9 + x ^ { 2 } = x ^ { 2 } + 2 x + 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.695,
            0.523,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Subtracting "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from both sides, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.72,
            0.549,
            0.738
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "9 = 2 x + 1 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.47,
            0.751,
            0.526,
            0.768
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "x = 4 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.773,
            0.511,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the depth of the lake is 4 units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.803,
            0.294,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.828,
            0.684,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the diagonal of a square with sidelength 5 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
